methods.explanation:
The gravel and dirt sections account for \(\frac13\) and \(\frac15\) of the whole trip. Thus the paved section is
\[
1-\frac13-\frac15
=\frac{15-5-3}{15}
=\frac7{15}
\]
of the trip. Since this positive fraction corresponds to \(20\) miles, dividing by it recovers the total distance:
\[
20\div\frac7{15}
=20\cdot\frac{15}{7}
=\boxed{\frac{300}{7}}\text{ miles}.
\]
The answer is choice E.
